# Motorhead body v1: Adder Mk2 (car 02), Base body (09-remaster 9.22 phase 6, #175). Game-space
# metres, x to the right, y up, z forward. Colours `r,g,b` are the MYO face tags before the
# repaint. Design choices unless marked [O].
#
# [O] cage 190 v / 228 p (190 welded), 0 open edges, 2 edges on more than 2 faces, 190/190
# mirror twins; 108 edges under 10 deg, 46 at 10-20, 258 over 20; edge min 0.044 median 0.292 m.
# The two edges on more than 2 faces are the mirror bases, 4 faces each: the housing's 8/12
# (-x) and 14/18 (+x) meet the A-pillar panels 189/191 and 222/224 along one edge
# ((+-0.856 0.915 0.678) to (+-0.789 0.934 0.653)). No repeated face (unlike the Serpent's
# 95 = 89); the bevel and the corner fans cope as they are, mesh check non-manifold 0.
# Box x +-1.069, y 0.226-1.244, z -1.987..1.987; hubs x +-0.75 (PhyWheel 0.6 x 1.25), z 1.22 /
# -1.42. A blue wedge coupe: Colour1 15 53 123 (54 faces: bonnet, front fenders, the upper
# flanks), Colour2 23 91 174 (41: the rear haunches and deck, the roof, the front lip and the
# sills) and Colour3 155 159 164 (36: the mirrors, the canopy's pillars, the diagonal stripe).
# The arch tunnels and the underside (Underred) are 0 0 0 (61 faces). The textured parts
# (Spoller 24-30 = the spoiler on the rear deck, the side intake 44-49 / 137 / 138, the Grill1
# panel 20/22/23 between the tail lamps, the Oklog2 roof logo 39) stay as in the original
# until the Full body. Stance kept as the original's (drop 0) for the first pass.
Body bevel=0.015 segments=3 bevel_tol=0.001 smooth_deg=10 arch_step_deg=7.5 arch_clearance=0.035 arch_lip=0.02 drop=0

# [O] the mirror faces are the white 216 217 218 quads 5/6 on the back of the housings
# (x 0.856-1.069, y 0.915-1.007, z 0.637-0.678)
MirrorGlass rgb=216,217,218

# [O] glass is 75 92 107 (10 faces, type 8/9: windscreen 31/36/37, side windows 33/34 and
# 40/41, rear window 35/42/43); the rest as the Titan's
Glass rgb=75,92,107 frame=0.02 inset=0.015 tint=0.6

# [O] headlights: one Ooflight quad a side, tag 125 127 104 (157/158, x 0.516-0.828, y 0.479-0.603,
# z 1.668-1.908, facing forward and out, n 0.58 0.13 0.80); halo 0/1 runs it from (0.58 0.51 1.89)
# to (0.82 0.56 1.71), rgb fd ff b3. Design choice: a reflector bowl with three bulbs along the
# slim lens and a daytime light bar along its bottom edge.
Lamp from=125,127,104 frame=0.008 inset=0.03 tint=0.45 kind=reflector count=3 rows=1 pitch=0 bulb=0.011 led_inset=0.03
Led pts=0,0;0.95,0 repeat=1 step=0,0 style=bar width=0.025 margin=0 clip=0 halo=1
# [O] tail lights: one Obblight quad a side, tag 127 49 19 (19/21, x 0.55-0.897, y 0.804-0.933,
# z -1.817..-1.566, on the sloping rear deck, facing up, back and out, n 0.32 0.78 -0.53); halo
# 2/3 runs it from (0.575 0.875 -1.75) to (0.85 0.85 -1.625), rgb ff 24 24. Design choice: three
# light bars across the lens (frame units = the lens's width, about 0.35 m).
Lamp from=127,49,19 frame=0.012 inset=0.02 tint=0.55 kind=leds led_inset=0.03
Led pts=0,0.03;0.95,0.03 repeat=3 step=0,0.08 style=bar width=0.03 margin=0 clip=0 halo=1

# [O] the bonnet's nose end: three black quads 0-2 (x +-0.267, y 0.651-0.694, z 1.652-1.764, facing
# up and back) between the channel's walls 3/4 (flat black triangles, kept as they are).
# Design choice: the mouth an empty recess, like the ASC's bonnet channel.
Vent from=0,0,0 lo=0,0.6,1.6 hi=0.3,0.72,1.8 rgb=3,3,5 frame=0.008 inset=0.03 tint=0.5 kind=plain

# Second pass (#537, the user's request of 2026-11-16: smooth out the blocky, hard-edged body, a
# concept render of a rounded blue coupé as the inspiration). [O] The first pass faired only the
# front fenders and the rear haunches; the rest stayed flat facets with the 1.5 cm bevel: 258 of
# the cage's 414 edges fold over 20 deg, among them the nose's leading edge 152/214 (58.5 deg, from
# the centre (0 0.51 1.983) to the headlamp's inner corner), the tail panel to the bumper 205/212
# (42.7), the rear corners 198/217 (49.7) and the fender crowns 220/225, 221/226, 202/211 (41-48).
# Design choice (like the Serpent's and the ASC's third passes): one zone over all paint (the
# three colours) and both lamp lenses, `max_deg` 65 so every paint fold rounds, `round` 0.2. The
# lenses are in the zone because the headlamp's corners end five of the nose's folds (152/214,
# 151/160, 155/160, 195/200, 195/227) and the tail lamp's five of the haunch's and the tail's
# (198/212, 198/217, 197/213, 197/217, 213/218): out of the zone they are pinned points and the
# plate pinches round them. Left out, so they keep their outlines: the mirrors 7-18 (Colour3 too;
# their centroids, |x| 0.83-1.02, y 0.94-1.0, z 0.66-0.68, fall in no box), the glass, the black
# arch tunnels, the underside, the bonnet scoop, the side intake, the spoiler and the Grill1 panel.
# - The silver blade 137/138 (n 0.88 -0.41 -0.24, the sloped step from the door 202 to the
#   recessed side 206 ahead of the intake) is out too, carved by the boxes' gap at z -0.22..-0.2
#   (its centroid is at z -0.212). [O] All four of its corners lie on faces out of the zone (the
#   black ledge 50/51 under it, the intake's top 52), so rounding its folds to the door (28.6 deg)
#   and to 206 (25.6) left a dimple at each end, with `round` 0.2 and still at 0.06. Out of the
#   zone it is a crisp flat panel the door and 206 round into, as the concept's silver blade.
# - The shoulder (the chamfer 211/226 between the door/fender side and the top 222/224) and the
#   window sill 222 with the A-pillar's foot 71 get their own boxes, first so they win, with
#   `round` 0.06 at the mirrors rising to 0.2 by z 0 and z 1.1 (a ramp along z). [O] The shoulder's
#   upper fold (211/222 28.1 deg, 224/226 36.7) runs through the mirror base's corner (0.856 0.915
#   0.678), a pinned point (the mirror's faces are out), and at 0.2 it dented the shoulder under
#   the mirror; the plate also pulled the whole fold 4-5 cm in (plan cut at y 0.8) and the door
#   below it went concave by up to 4 cm. [D] With the ramp the shoulder line keeps its place in
#   plan beside the mirror (z 0.4-0.85, plan cut at y 0.8) and eases into the 0.2 rounding either
#   side (4.5 cm in at z -0.2, as before); the door below it crowns out up to 2.2 cm (z 0.5, y 0.6).
# - [D] `round` 0.3 everywhere pulled the nose's centre in further and broke its reflections up;
#   rounding never adds volume, so the crown the concept shows (wings over a lower bonnet, a fuller
#   nose) is left for `Warp`s / `Push`es (#537 phase 2).
Smooth from=15,53,123;23,91,174;155,159,164;125,127,104;127,49,19 lo=0.68,0.84,0.04;0.68,0.93,0;0,0,0.75;0,0,-2.1;0,0,-0.2;0,0,0.6 hi=0.92,0.93,1;0.92,1.05,0.55;1.1,1.3,2.1;1.1,1.3,-0.22;1.1,1.3,0.6;1.1,0.93,0.75 max_deg=65;65;65;65;65;65 step=0.025 loose=0 round=0.2@0:0.06@0.5:0.06@0.85:0.2@1.1;0.2@0:0.06@0.5:0.06@0.85:0.2@1.1;0.2;0.2;0.2;0.2
# [O] The glass is flat facets too: the windscreen's centre 36 folds 23.5 deg to its sides 37/31,
# the rear window 42/43 11.8, the side windows 40/41 2.6. Design choice (#537, as the Serpent's and
# the ASC's canopies): one zone, faired before the glass is recessed, with a longer `round` than
# the paint's so the windscreen reads as one even curve.
Smooth from=75,92,107 lo=0,0.85,-1.2 hi=0.8,1.3,1.2 max_deg=30 step=0.025 loose=0 round=0.3

# Every edge cut and every face remeshed at 4 cm, like the Titan, the ASC and the Resonic (#213,
# #172, #173): the bevel strips' rows and the long fans over the big panels are slivers otherwise.
Refine step=0.04

# Second pass, the user's follow-up (#537, 2026-11-16: the front lip's bottom edge, seen from above,
# round instead of angled). [O] The lip's bottom edge is the zone's outline (the underside, black
# like the tunnels, scoop and intake, is out of it), so it keeps the cage's plan polygon: the
# centre (0 0.226 1.987), P1 (0.606 1.912), P2 (0.813 1.762) and the arch's front corner P3
# (0.849 1.599), turning 29 and 42 deg at P1 and P2 (and 14 at the centre). [D] Plan sections of
# the exported body: the turn within 2.5 cm at P2 is 43 deg at the bottom, 26 at y 0.25, 14 at
# y 0.27 and 7 from y 0.31 up, where the zone has rounded the corner to about 0.4 m.
# Design choice: two `Warp`s after the refine map the bottom edge onto one arc of radius 0.40 m
# tangent to the front segment and to the side P2-P3 (from x 0.504 on the front to 1.5 cm short
# of P3, cutting P1 in 1.4 cm and P2 3.4 cm), and round the centre's V with R 1.5 m (the nose's
# bottom 1.1 cm back). The first moves z as a table over x (the front corner), the second x as a
# table over z (the side corner, where a z move would only slide the points along the side); both
# meet at the arc's touch point on P1-P2 (0.690 1.851). The tables are the arc minus the polygon,
# every 2 cm with nodes on the corners (a warp's weight is smooth, so it cancels a corner only
# where a node sits on it). Both fade over the lip's bottom 8 cm (1, 0.8, 0.5, 0.25, 0.08, 0 at
# y 0.226-0.31, the corner's measured fade); nothing behind z 1.614 moves, so the arch (its front
# wall at z 1.599) stays.
# [D] Only the lip and the underside's front edge move (up to 3.0 cm); bottom edge's worst turn
# within 2.5 cm 43 -> 7 deg; 1-2.5 cm above it 13-15 deg remain, 4 deg concave, inside the 1.5 cm
# bevel (the lip's corner folds slant back as they rise; slower or faster fades, per corner too,
# were worse). Designed with a scratch script (arc, tables) from these numbers.
Warp by=0,0,-0.0139 x=0,0.8219;0.005,0.778;0.01,0.7354;0.015,0.6939;0.02,0.6537;0.04,0.5047;0.06,0.3748;0.08,0.2641;0.1,0.1727;0.12,0.1006;0.14,0.0478;0.16,0.0144;0.18,0.0004;0.1842,0;0.5043,0;0.52,0.0229;0.54,0.1189;0.56,0.292;0.58,0.545;0.6,0.8819;0.606,1;0.62,0.7034;0.64,0.3611;0.66,0.122;0.68,0;0.6998,0 y=0.226,1;0.235,0.8;0.25,0.5;0.27,0.25;0.29,0.08;0.31,0 z=1.7,0;1.8,1
Warp by=-0.0337,0,0 x=0.55,0;0.66,1 y=0.226,1;0.235,0.8;0.25,0.5;0.27,0.25;0.29,0.08;0.31,0 z=1.5939,0;1.6139,0;1.6339,0.0161;1.6539,0.0654;1.6739,0.1494;1.6939,0.2702;1.7139,0.4304;1.7339,0.6335;1.7539,0.8839;1.762,1;1.7739,0.7784;1.7939,0.4554;1.8139,0.2042;1.8339,0.0407;1.8515,0
